  "bone_fixups": {
    "_why": "Meshy put the left elbow 0.14 behind the back (y +0.097 while shoulder and hand sit at y -0.04..-0.07), so the forearm bone ran diagonally through the skirt side and the upper arm through the hair; vertices along that path kept arm weights and rose with the arm. Elbows are moved onto the shoulder-hand line, pushed 0.035 outward. Moving a joint does not deform the rest mesh. Hand bones were as long as forearms and pointed down through the skirt hem; shortened to chibi hand length so the skirt side is no longer 'near the hand'.",
